<title>SPAIN: Spain's Amper Q1 1997 net profit up 88 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Amper Q1 1997 net profit up 88 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish telecommunications equipment firm Amper results in first quarter 1997 (in million pesetas, unless stated):</p>
<p>    Net profit		     1,570	    up    88 pct</p>
<p>    Ordinary results	     1,059	    up    33 pct</p>
<p>    Cash Flow			2,058	    up    44 pct</p>
<p>    Turnover			 7,674	    down  24 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it will pay a final dividend of 45 pesetas per share versus 1996 results, for a total dividend of 85 pesetas. Amper has not paid dividends since 1990.</p>
<p>The group adedd that turnover declined after Amper sold a 80 percent stake of Amper Elasa to Siemens at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
